l Analysis Plan and data was not collected for primary and secondary endpoints..\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 1 through week 36\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Pozelimab and Cemdisiran\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Anti-C5 Standard-of-care\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Fatigue as Measured by the Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy-Fatigue (FACIT-Fatigue) Scale From Baseline to Week 36\",\"description\":\"The FACIT-Fatigue is a 13 item, self-administered clinical outcome assessment (COA) assessing an individual's level of fatigue during their usual daily activities over the past week. This questionnaire is part of the FACIT measurement system, a compilation of questions measuring health related quality of life (QoL) in patients with cancer and other chronic illnesses. The FACIT-Fatigue assesses the level of fatigue using a Likert scale ranging from 0 (not at all) to 4 (very much). Scores range from 0 to 52, with higher scores indicating greater fatigue.\",\"populationDescription\":\"Due to Early Termination, this endpoint was removed from the Statistical Analysis Plan and data was not collected for primary and secondary endpoints..\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"timeFrame\":\"From baseline to week 36\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Pozelimab and Cemdisiran\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Anti-C5 Standard-of-care\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Physical Function (PF) Score on the European Organization for Research and Treatment of Cancer Quality-of-Life Questionnaire Core 30 Items (EORTC-QLQ-C30) From Baseline to Week 36\",\"description\":\"EORTC-QLQ-C30 is a 30-item subject self-report questionnaire composed of both multi-item and single scales, including global health status/quality of life, functional Scales (physical, role, emotional, cognitive, and social), symptom scales (fatigue, nausea and vomiting, and pain), and 6 single items (dyspnea, insomnia, appetite loss, constipation, diarrhea, and financial difficulties). Participants rate items on a 4-point scale, with 1 as \\\"not at all\\\" and 4 as \\\"very much.\\\"\",\"populationDescription\":\"Due to Early Termination, this endpoint was removed from the Statistical Analysis Plan and data was not collected for primary and secondary endpoints..\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"timeFrame\":\"From baseline to week 36\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Pozelimab and Cemdisiran\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Anti-C5 Standard-of-care\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Change in Global Health Status (GHS)/QoL Scale Score on the EORTC-QLQ-C30 From Baseline to Week 36\",\"description\":\"EORTC-QLQ-C30 is a 30-item subject self-report questionnaire composed of both multi-item and single scales, including global health status/quality of life, functional Scales (physical, role, emotional, cognitive, and social), symptom scales (fatigue, nausea and vomiting, and pain), and 7 single items (dyspnea, insomnia, appetite loss, constipation, diarrhea, sleep and financial difficulties). Participants rate items on a 4-point scale, with 1 as \\\"not at all\\\" and 4 as \\\"very much.\\\"\",\"populationDescription\":\"Due to Early Termination, this endpoint was removed from the Statistical Analysis Plan and data was not collected for primary and secondary endpoints..\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"timeFrame\":\"From baseline to week 36\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Pozelimab and Cemdisiran\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Anti-C5 Standard-of-care\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Rate of RBCs Transfused Per Protocol Algorithm After Day 1 Through Week 36\",\"description\":\"Per protocol algorithm\",\"populationDescription\":\"Due to Early Termination, this endpoint was removed from the Statistical Analysis Plan and data was not collected for primary and secondary endpoints.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"timeFrame\":\"Day 1 through week 36\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Pozelimab and Cemdisiran\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Anti-C5 Standard-of-care\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Rate of RBCs Transfused Per Protocol Algorithm From Week 4 Through Week 36\",\"description\":\"Per protocol algorithm\",\"populationDescription\":\"Due to Early Termination, this endpoint was removed from the Statistical Analysis Plan and data was not collected for primary and secondary endpoints.\",\"reportingStatus\":\"POSTED\",\"timeFrame\":\"Week 4 through week 36\",\"groups\":[{\"id\":\"OG000\",\"title\":\"Pozelimab and Cemdisiran\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"},{\"id\":\"OG001\",\"title\":\"Anti-C5 Standard-of-care\",\"description\":\"Randomized 1:1\"}],\"denoms\":[{\"units\":\"Participants\",\"counts\":[{\"groupId\":\"OG000\",\"value\":\"0\"},{\"groupId\":\"OG001\",\"value\":\"0\"}]}]},{\"type\":\"SECONDARY\",\"title\":\"Number of Units of RBCs Transfused Per Protocol Algorithm After 